<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<odoo>
    <!--
        Four example notices, one in each state, built in Python rather than
        written out here.

        Two of them need dates relative to now - one that has not started and
        one that has finished - and an XML record would freeze those at
        whenever the module happened to be installed, so the example set would
        be wrong by the next morning and the tabs it is meant to fill would be
        empty again.

        The method does nothing once a demo notice exists, so a shop that has
        written its own never sprouts examples. The three real notices in
        account_data.xml are left alone: those are content, not examples, and
        they sit under noupdate for that reason.

        Not noupdate: with it the function would only run on a fresh install,
        and a shop upgrading into this feature would never see the examples.
        The method guards itself instead, so running on every upgrade is safe
        and seeds exactly once.
    -->
    <data>
        <function model="mart369.notice" name="_mart369_load_notice_demo"/>
    </data>
</odoo>
